  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
  "modifications": [
    "Dependencies upgraded to Astro 7 and the current release of each package; the remark and rehype plugins run through the unified processor of @astrojs/markdown-remark (package.json, astro.config.mjs).",
    "Removed, with their dependencies: the PDF and PDF book export, the LaTeX export and import, the Notion import, the figure screenshot tool, the upstream template sync and the Hugging Face Space thumbnail script (scripts/, src/styles/_print-book.css).",
    "Removed the PDF download from the article header, with its showPdf and pdfProOnly frontmatter options (HeroArticle.astro, heroUtils.ts, pages/index.astro, _print.css).",
    "Removed the Svelte integration, which rendered no component, and remark-footnotes, whose [^name] footnotes the processor's GitHub-flavoured Markdown provides.",
    "Added plugins/remark/restore-text-directives.mjs, which keeps text such as :8031 in http://127.0.0.1:8031/ as written, because remark-directive 4 reads it as a directive.",
    "Adapted to Astro 7 and KaTeX 0.19: JavaScript comments instead of HTML comments inside expressions (Note.astro), KaTeX's prefixed class names (_base.css, Footer.astro), compressHTML kept at true, and Gzip as the only precompression.",
    "Removed CSS that no browser applied: :global() selectors in global stylesheets (_layout.css, _mermaid.css), and the padding of the dataviz page that the global layout overrode (pages/dataviz.astro).",
    "Removed the import of the Source Sans Pro stylesheet from Google Fonts: its address answers HTTP 400, so no page ever loaded the font, and every page made the failing request (_base.css)."
  ],
